{"post": true, "caption": "In early 1720, Isaac Newton sold his South Sea Company shares at a big profit.\nThen the price kept soaring. He bought back in at a much higher price, and reportedly lost about £20,000 when it crashed.\nThe lesson: your exit rules have to hold even when everyone else seems to be getting rich.\nBe honest: have you ever jumped back into a trade you already sold? Yes or no.\n\nEducation only. Not financial advice.\n\n#CandleAndCode #StoryTime #TradingPsychology #FOMO #MarketHistory", "tag": "STORY TIME", "footer": "Education only. Not financial advice.", "bpm": 92, "scenes": [
